+# Privacy audit – The Daily Grind
+
+## Data collection
+- No forms, scripts, cookies, localStorage, analytics, or trackers. The page collects no user data.
+- Any future form must collect the minimum data, explain why inline, and offer guest checkout.
+
+## Third parties
+| Origin | Use | Mitigation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| images.unsplash.com | Hero background image | Only allowed origin (`img-src`); no referrer sent (`same-origin` policy). **Recommended:** self-host the image and drop the origin from CSP. |
+
+No third-party scripts, fonts, or embeds.
+
+## Hardening applied
+- Inline CSS moved to `/styles.css` and the inline style attribute removed, so CSP needs no `'unsafe-inline'`.
+- CSP via `<meta>` (deny-by-default, `script-src 'none'`); full header set in `_headers` adds `frame-ancestors`, Trusted Types, HSTS, nosniff, Permissions-Policy, COOP/CORP.
+- Referrer policy `same-origin`.
+- `Clear-Site-Data` on `/logout`; session cookies should use `__Host-` prefix, `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax`.
+- Logout should be a POST endpoint server-side to avoid CSRF/prefetch logouts (link is `rel="nofollow"` for now).
+- Note: `npm start` (statikk) does not read `_headers`; configure headers at the host/CDN.
